The Challenge 
 We are looking for a Solutions Architect or a Technical Lead seeking to transition into an architecture role and join our team. The successful candidate will contribute to the design, evolution, and delivery of robust, high-performing, secure, and scalable solutions, primarily in the healthcare sector.
 This role is intended for a technical, curious, pragmatic, and hands-on professional who can bridge the gap between target architecture, product requirements, and the realities faced by development teams. The successful candidate will actively contribute to technical decisions, solution implementation, software quality improvements, and the adoption of new approaches, particularly in artificial intelligence.
 Key Responsibilities 
 With the guidance and support of the architecture team, the successful candidate will:
 Contribute to the design and evolution of solution architectures in collaboration with architects, development teams, Product Owners, and product leaders;
 Participate in defining the technical direction for web solutions, APIs, integrations, distributed systems, and highly available environments;
 Play an active, hands-on role in validating technology choices, developing proofs of concept, prototyping, and providing technical guidance to teams;
 Contribute to the integration of artificial intelligence capabilities, including the use of AI tools to accelerate development, improve quality, automate certain tasks, and enhance products;
 Help teams design solutions that are high-performing, stable, secure, maintainable, and capable of supporting increased usage volumes;
 Participate in the analysis and resolution of complex issues related to performance, stability, scalability, integration, and solution operations;
 Participate in code reviews, architecture reviews, and technical discussions to ensure alignment with quality, security, and maintainability standards;
 Contribute to improving practices related to web development, continuous integration, automated deployment, observability, and DevSecOps;
 Document architecture decisions, integration flows, technical trade-offs, and the non-functional impacts of solutions;
 Explain technical issues clearly to non-technical stakeholders and help build consensus around decisions;
 Collaborate with product teams to ensure that non-functional requirements—including performance, availability, security, operability, maintainability, and scalability—are considered from the design stage onward.
What You Bring 
 A bachelor’s degree in computer science, software engineering, computer engineering, or equivalent experience;
 Experience as a Solutions Architect or significant experience as a Technical Lead, Senior Developer, or in a similar role;
 A strong interest in solution architecture, application modernization, applied artificial intelligence, and software development best practices;
 The ability to quickly understand existing systems, identify technical challenges, and recommend practical improvements;
 A hands-on approach, with the ability to read code, contribute technically, develop prototypes, and support teams throughout implementation;
 Sound technical judgment and the ability to balance quality, simplicity, cost, timelines, risk, and business value;
 Excellent collaboration, communication, and influencing skills;
 Curiosity, autonomy, thoroughness, and a strong willingness to learn;
 A good understanding of application security principles;
 Knowledge of the healthcare sector is a significant asset;
 Excellent written and verbal communication skills in both French and English.
 Desired Technical Skills and Experience 
 Experience or a strong interest in several of the following areas:
 Modern web development: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, front-end frameworks, user experience, and UI integration;
 Back-end development: Java, .NET, REST services, APIs, application architecture, and systems integration;
 Databases and optimization: Oracle, SQL, performance analysis, indexing, complex queries, and high-volume data processing;
 Performance, stability, and scalability of high-volume solutions;
 API architecture, application decoupling, modularization, distributed services, and integration with existing systems;
 Healthcare integration standards such as HL7v2, HL7v3, FHIR, IHE, or other relevant standards;
 Artificial intelligence applied to software development, automation, data analysis, semantic search, or user assistance;
 DevSecOps practices, continuous integration, automated deployment, and dependency management;
 Tools such as Git, Azure DevOps, Artifactory, Snyk, FOSSA, SonarQube, Ansible, PowerShell, or equivalent technologies;
 Application security, identity management, authentication, authorization, secrets management, auditing, and compliance;
 Observability, logging, monitoring, alerting, production diagnostics, and improved operability;
 Deployment of highly available solutions in distributed, cloud, hybrid, or on-premises environments.
 What We Value Most 
 We are looking for someone who enjoys developing an in-depth understanding of systems, wants to help improve solution quality, and is eager to progressively develop an architectural mindset. This role requires both the ability to think strategically about the target architecture and a willingness to remain closely connected to the code, the teams, and the realities of solution delivery.
 The ideal candidate is a natural technical leader who can influence others through credibility, example, and collaboration while progressively developing a broader vision of our solutions, products, and their long-term evolution.
Why join LGI? 
 A workplace built on trust, autonomy and collaboration 
 The opportunity to grow, perform and work alongside curious and talented colleagues 
 A continuous learning culture with dedicated training time, a renowed skills development platform and access to cutting-edge tools 
 Stimulating projects that advance healthcare technology and support the work of over 320,000 professionals, benefiting more than 6 million patients 
 A comprehensive benefits package including group insurance from day one, a group RRSP with employer contributions, 24/7 telemedicine, an employee and family assistance program, and a minimum of 3 weeks vacation per year 
 At LGI Healthcare Solutions, we value diversity and equal access to employment. 
 If this position interests you, we’d be happy to tell you more about the role, the team, and life at LGI Healthcare Solutions.
 Apply now!

